{"code": "ko", "name": "Korean", "native": "한국어", "phase": 1, "medium": "en", "file_level": "B2", "level": {"title": "Advanced: conditionals, honorifics, debate, culture", "goals": ["Use -(으)면 and -(으)ㅂ시다 naturally", "Honor elders with full -시- speech", "Discuss Korean culture with real fluency"], "units": [{"id": "B2-U1", "title": "Conditionals and plans", "lessons": [{"id": "B2-U1-L1", "title": "If: -(으)면", "learn": "The all-round IF! 먹으면 (if I eat), 가면 (if I go), 비가 오면 (if it rains). Vowel-stems: -면, consonants: -으면! 와도 (even if): 와도 가요 = Even if it rains, I go!", "vocab": [{"t": "하면", "r": "hamyeon", "en": "if (I) do", "pos": "phrase"}, {"t": "가면", "r": "gamyeon", "en": "if (I) go", "pos": "phrase"}, {"t": "먹으면", "r": "meog-eumyeon", "en": "if (I) eat", "pos": "phrase"}, {"t": "오면", "r": "omyeon", "en": "if (I) come", "pos": "phrase"}, {"t": "비가 오면", "r": "bi-ga omyeon", "en": "if it rains", "pos": "phrase"}, {"t": "거든", "r": "geodeun", "en": "since (reason)", "pos": "suffix"}, {"t": "만일", "r": "man-il", "en": "if by chance", "pos": "adverb"}, {"t": "만약", "r": "man-yak", "en": "if / in case", "pos": "adverb"}], "grammar": {"title": "-(으)면 (if) · -아/어도 (even if)", "explain": "먹으면 (if eat), 가면 (if go). 비가 오면 안 가요 (if it rains, I won't go). 와도 가요 (even if rains, go)! 공부하면 알아요 (if you study, you know)!", "pattern": "(으)면 · 아/어도", "examples": [{"t": "비가 오면 안 가요.", "r": "bi-ga omyeon an gayo.", "en": "If it rains, I won't go."}, {"t": "공부하면 알아요.", "r": "gongbu-hamyeon al-ayo.", "en": "If you study, you know."}, {"t": "와도 가요!", "r": "wado gayo!", "en": "Even if it rains, I'll go!"}], "mistakes": ["Saying 먹면 — consonants: 먹으면!", "Saying 가으면 — vowels: 가면!"]}, "dialogue": [{"sp": "미나", "t": "내일 비가 오면 어떻게 해요?", "r": "nae-il bi-ga omyeon eotteoke haeyo?", "en": "If it rains tomorrow, what will you do?"}, {"sp": "지훈", "t": "와도 가요!", "r": "wado gayo!", "en": "Even if it rains, I'll go!"}, {"sp": "미나", "t": "공부하면 알아요!", "r": "gongbu-hamyeon al-ayo!", "en": "If you study, you'll know!"}, {"sp": "지훈", "t": "열심히 할게요!", "r": "yeolsimhi halgeyo!", "en": "I'll work hard! (promise)"}], "practice": [{"type": "translate_en", "q": "Say: If it rains, I won't go", "answer": "비가 오면 안 가요"}, {"type": "fill", "q": "와___ 가요! (even if)", "answer": "도"}, {"type": "choose", "q": "'If you study, you know' is…", "options": ["공부하고 알아요", "공부하면 알아요", "공부해도 알아요", "공부하니까 알았어요"], "answer": "공부하면 알아요"}, {"type": "reorder", "q": "Order: 안 가요 / 오면 / 비가", "answer": "비가 오면 안 가요"}, {"type": "speak", "q": "Say aloud: 비가 오면 안 가요.", "answer": "비가 오면 안 가요."}], "quiz": [{"q": "-(으)면 means…", "options": ["because", "if", "although", "until"], "answer": 1, "why": "오면 = if it comes."}, {"q": "-아/어도 means…", "options": ["if", "even if", "because", "whenever"], "answer": 1, "why": "와도 = even if rains."}, {"q": "Consonant-stems take…", "options": ["-면", "-으면", "-려면", "-으면만"], "answer": 1, "why": "먹으면 — 을 after consonants."}, {"q": "만약 means…", "options": ["always", "if / in case", "never", "must"], "answer": 1, "why": "만약 = if-by-chance."}, {"q": "열심히 할게요 is…", "options": ["a question", "a promise", "past", "a command"], "answer": 1, "why": "-ㄹ게요 = I promise to!"}], "flashcards": "auto:vocab", "worksheet": {"title": "Conditionals worksheet", "tasks": [{"instruction": "Translate to Korean.", "items": ["if (I) go", "if it rains", "even if"], "key": ["가면", "비가 오면", "-아/어도"]}, {"instruction": "If-plans.", "items": ["If it rains, I won't go", "Even if it rains, I'll go", "If you study, you know"], "key": ["비가 오면 안 가요", "와도 가요", "공부하면 알아요"]}, {"instruction": "Ask.", "items": ["If it rains tomorrow, what will you do?", "I'll work hard!"], "key": ["내일 비가 오면 어떻게 해요", "열심히 할게요"]}]}}, {"id": "B2-U1-L2", "title": "Let's and decisions: ㅂ시다/기로", "learn": "Formal LET'S! 갑시다 (let's go), 먹읍시다 (let's eat), 합시다! Decide: -기로 했어요 (I decided to): 가기로 했어요! Plans set: 예정이에요. Rally the group!", "vocab": [{"t": "합시다", "r": "hapsida", "en": "let's do", "pos": "verb"}, {"t": "갑시다", "r": "gapsida", "en": "let's go", "pos": "verb"}, {"t": "먹읍시다", "r": "meog-eupsida", "en": "let's eat", "pos": "verb"}, {"t": "봅시다", "r": "bopsida", "en": "let's see", "pos": "verb"}, {"t": "하기로 했어요", "r": "hagiro haess-eoyo", "en": "decided to do", "pos": "phrase"}, {"t": "가기로 했어요", "r": "kagiro haess-eoyo", "en": "decided to go", "pos": "phrase"}, {"t": "작정", "r": "jakjeong", "en": "intention", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "예정", "r": "yejeong", "en": "schedule", "pos": "noun"}], "grammar": {"title": "-(으)ㅂ시다 + -기로 했어요", "explain": "갑시다! (let's go!), 먹읍시다! Plans decided: 한국에 가기로 했어요 (I decided to go to Korea). 예정: 갈 예정이에요 (scheduled to go)!", "pattern": "(으)ㅂ시다 · 기로 했어요", "examples": [{"t": "같이 먹읍시다!", "r": "gachi meog-eupsida!", "en": "Let's eat together!"}, {"t": "한국에 가기로 했어요.", "r": "hangug-e kagiro haess-eoyo.", "en": "I decided to go to Korea."}, {"t": "갈 예정이에요.", "r": "gal yejeong-ieyo.", "en": "I'm scheduled to go."}], "mistakes": ["Saying 가시다 — let's-go: 갑시다!", "Saying 가기로 해요 for past decisions — decided: 했어요!"]}, "dialogue": [{"sp": "지훈", "t": "내일 뭐 해요?", "r": "nae-il mwo haeyo?", "en": "What will you do tomorrow?"}, {"sp": "미나", "t": "서울에 가기로 했어요!", "r": "seoul-e kagiro haess-eoyo!", "en": "I decided to go to Seoul!"}, {"sp": "지훈", "t": "좋아요! 같이 갑시다!", "r": "jo-ayo! gachi gapsida!", "en": "Good! Let's go together!"}, {"sp": "미나", "t": "꼭!", "r": "kkok!", "en": "Definitely!"}], "practice": [{"type": "translate_en", "q": "Say: Let's eat together!", "answer": "같이 먹읍시다"}, {"type": "fill", "q": "한국에 가___ 했어요. (decided to)", "answer": "기로"}, {"type": "choose", "q": "'I decided to go to Korea' is…", "options": ["한국에 가려고 해요", "한국에 가기로 했어요", "한국에 갑시다", "한국에 갈까요"], "answer": "한국에 가기로 했어요"}, {"type": "reorder", "q": "Order: 먹읍시다 / 같이", "answer": "같이 먹읍시다"}, {"type": "speak", "q": "Say aloud: 같이 먹읍시다!", "answer": "같이 먹읍시다!"}], "quiz": [{"q": "ㅂ시다 means…", "options": ["must", "let's (formal)", "want", "can"], "answer": 1, "why": "갑시다 = let's go."}, {"q": "가기로 했어요 means…", "options": ["I plan to go", "I decided to go", "let's go", "I must go"], "answer": 1, "why": "기로 했어요 = decided."}, {"q": "갈 예정이에요 means…", "options": ["want to go", "scheduled to go", "decided to go", "must go"], "answer": 1, "why": "예정 = schedule."}, {"q": "Casual let's-go is…", "options": ["갑시다", "가자", "가기로", "가려고"], "answer": 1, "why": "가자 — friends' form."}, {"q": "꼭! means…", "options": ["maybe", "definitely", "never", "sorry"], "answer": 1, "why": "꼭 = surely/definitely!"}], "flashcards": "auto:vocab", "worksheet": {"title": "Decisions worksheet", "tasks": [{"instruction": "Translate to Korean.", "items": ["let's (formal)", "decided to go", "schedule"], "key": ["ㅂ시다", "가기로 했어요", "예정"]}, {"instruction": "Decide.", "items": ["Let's eat together!", "I decided to go to Korea", "I'm scheduled to go"], "key": ["같이 먹읍시다", "한국에 가기로 했어요", "갈 예정이에요"]}, {"instruction": "Invite.", "items": ["Let's go together!", "Definitely!"], "key": ["같이 갑시다", "꼭"]}]}}]}, {"id": "B2-U2", "title": "Honorifics and debate", "lessons": [{"id": "B2-U2-L1", "title": "Full honorifics: -시-", "learn": "Honor in every verb! -시- infix: 가세요 (honorific go), 드세요 (honorific eat), 주무세요 (honorific sleep), 계세요 (honorific be). Honorific nouns: 말씀 (words), 성함 (name), 댁 (home)!", "vocab": [{"t": "하세요", "r": "haseyo", "en": "honorific do", "pos": "verb"}, {"t": "드세요", "r": "deuseyo", "en": "honorific eat", "pos": "verb"}, {"t": "주무세요", "r": "jumuseyo", "en": "honorific sleep", "pos": "verb"}, {"t": "계세요", "r": "gyeseyo", "en": "honorific be", "pos": "verb"}, {"t": "말씀", "r": "malsseum", "en": "honorific words", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "성함", "r": "seongham", "en": "honorific name", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "댁", "r": "daek", "en": "honorific home", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "드리다", "r": "deu-rida", "en": "humble give", "pos": "verb"}], "grammar": {"title": "-시- infix + honorific nouns", "explain": "선생님이 계세요? (Is the teacher there?). 잡수세요 = honorific eat (alt). 말씀하세요 (please speak, honored). Humble ME: 드리다 (I humbly give)!", "pattern": "-시- for elders · humble 드리다/저 for self", "examples": [{"t": "선생님이 계세요?", "r": "seonsaeng-nim-i gyeseyo?", "en": "Is the teacher there? (honorific)"}, {"t": "많이 드세요!", "r": "man-i deuseyo!", "en": "Eat a lot! (honorific)"}, {"t": "제가 해 드릴게요.", "r": "jega hae deuilgeyo.", "en": "I'll do it for you. (humble)"}], "mistakes": ["Using -시- for YOURSELF — honorifics elevate OTHERS!", "Saying 이름 to elders — their name: 성함!"]}, "dialogue": [{"sp": "미나", "t": "선생님이 계세요?", "r": "seonsaeng-nim-i gyeseyo?", "en": "Is the teacher there? (honorific)"}, {"sp": "지훈", "t": "네, 계세요!", "r": "ne, gyeseyo!", "en": "Yes, (honorific) here!"}, {"sp": "미나", "t": "많이 드세요!", "r": "man-i deuseyo!", "en": "Eat a lot!"}, {"sp": "지훈", "t": "대단히 감사합니다!", "r": "daedanhi gamsahamnida!", "en": "Thank you very much!"}], "practice": [{"type": "translate_en", "q": "Say (honorific): Is the teacher there?", "answer": "선생님이 계세요?"}, {"type": "fill", "q": "많이 ___! (honorific eat)", "answer": "드세요"}, {"type": "choose", "q": "Humble 'I'll do it for you' is…", "options": ["제가 해요", "제가 해 드릴게요", "제가 하세요", "제가 할 수 있어요"], "answer": "제가 해 드릴게요"}, {"type": "reorder", "q": "Order: 계세요 / 선생님이", "answer": "선생님이 계세요"}, {"type": "speak", "q": "Say aloud: 선생님이 계세요?", "answer": "선생님이 계세요?"}], "quiz": [{"q": "-시- elevates…", "options": ["myself", "others (elders)", "things", "animals"], "answer": 1, "why": "Honorific for respected others."}, {"q": "드세요 means…", "options": ["eat (humble)", "eat (honorific)", "eat (plain)", "eat (baby)"], "answer": 1, "why": "드세요 = respectful eat."}, {"q": "주무세요 is honorific…", "options": ["eat", "sleep", "go", "speak"], "answer": 1, "why": "주무세요 = honored sleep."}, {"q": "성함 is honorific…", "options": ["home", "name", "words", "food"], "answer": 1, "why": "성함 = honored name."}, {"q": "드리다 means…", "options": ["honorific eat", "humble give", "honorific go", "humble say"], "answer": 1, "why": "드리다 = I humbly give."}], "flashcards": "auto:vocab", "worksheet": {"title": "Honorifics worksheet", "tasks": [{"instruction": "Translate to Korean.", "items": ["honorific be", "honorific eat", "humble give"], "key": ["계세요", "드세요", "드리다"]}, {"instruction": "Honor elders.", "items": ["Is the teacher there? (honorific)", "Eat a lot! (honorific)", "I'll do it for you (humble)"], "key": ["선생님이 계세요", "많이 드세요", "제가 해 드릴게요"]}, {"instruction": "Thank deeply.", "items": ["Thank you very much!", "Eat a lot! (honorific)"], "key": ["대단히 감사합니다", "많이 드세요"]}]}}, {"id": "B2-U2-L2", "title": "Debate connectors", "learn": "Argue elegantly! 하지만 (but/however), 그래서 (so), 즉 (in other words), 예를 들어 (for example), 게다가 (besides), 결국 (after all). Chain: 예를 들어…게다가…그래서…!", "vocab": [{"t": "하지만", "r": "hajiman", "en": "but / however", "pos": "conjunction"}, {"t": "그래서", "r": "geuraeseo", "en": "so / therefore", "pos": "conjunction"}, {"t": "즉", "r": "jeuk", "en": "in other words", "pos": "adverb"}, {"t": "예를 들어", "r": "ye-reul deul-eo", "en": "for example", "pos": "phrase"}, {"t": "게다가", "r": "gedaga", "en": "besides / moreover", "pos": "conjunction"}, {"t": "더구나", "r": "deoguna", "en": "furthermore", "pos": "adverb"}, {"t": "요컨대", "r": "yogeondae", "en": "in short", "pos": "phrase"}, {"t": "결국", "r": "gyeolguk", "en": "after all / in the end", "pos": "adverb"}], "grammar": {"title": "Connector chains", "explain": "지하철은 편리해요. 하지만 복잡해요. 즉, 좋아요! (The subway is handy. But crowded. In short, good!). Start sentences with 하지만/그래서/즉!", "pattern": "…。하지만…。그래서…。", "examples": [{"t": "지하철은 편리해요. 하지만 복잡해요.", "r": "jihacheol-eun pyeollihaeyo. hajiman bokjapaeyo.", "en": "The subway is handy. However, it's crowded."}, {"t": "예를 들어, 서울은 커요.", "r": "ye-reul deul-eo, seoul-eun keoyo.", "en": "For example, Seoul is big."}, {"t": "즉, 지하철이 좋아요!", "r": "jeuk, jihacheol-i jo-ayo!", "en": "In short, the subway is good!"}], "mistakes": ["Saying 하지만 at sentence END — 하지만 starts sentences!", "Stacking 하지만…하지만 — vary with 게다가/즉!"]}, "dialogue": [{"sp": "미나", "t": "지하철은 편리해요. 하지만 복잡해요.", "r": "jihacheol-eun pyeollihaeyo. hajiman bokjapaeyo.", "en": "The subway is handy. However, it's crowded."}, {"sp": "지훈", "t": "하지만 차는 빨라요!", "r": "hajiman cha-neun ppallayo!", "en": "However, the car is fast!"}, {"sp": "미나", "t": "게다가 지하철이 싸요!", "r": "gedaga jihacheol-i ssayo!", "en": "Besides, the subway is cheap!"}, {"sp": "지훈", "t": "즉, 지하철이 좋아요!", "r": "jeuk, jihacheol-i jo-ayo!", "en": "In short, the subway is good!"}], "practice": [{"type": "translate_en", "q": "Say: In short, the subway is good!", "answer": "즉, 지하철이 좋아요"}, {"type": "fill", "q": "___ 차는 빨라요! (However)", "answer": "하지만"}, {"type": "choose", "q": "'For example' is…", "options": ["즉", "예를 들어", "게다가", "결국"], "answer": "예를 들어"}, {"type": "reorder", "q": "Order: 지하철이 좋아요 / 즉", "answer": "즉 지하철이 좋아요"}, {"type": "speak", "q": "Say aloud: 즉, 지하철이 좋아요!", "answer": "즉, 지하철이 좋아요!"}], "quiz": [{"q": "하지만 means…", "options": ["therefore", "but / however", "for example", "in short"], "answer": 1, "why": "하지만 = however."}, {"q": "그래서 means…", "options": ["however", "so / therefore", "for example", "besides"], "answer": 1, "why": "그래서 = so."}, {"q": "예를 들어 means…", "options": ["in short", "for example", "however", "after all"], "answer": 1, "why": "예를 들어 = for example."}, {"q": "즉 means…", "options": ["however", "in other words", "besides", "after all"], "answer": 1, "why": "즉 = in short/words."}, {"q": "하지만 goes…", "options": ["at sentence end", "at sentence start", "in questions", "nowhere"], "answer": 1, "why": "하지만, … — starts!"}], "flashcards": "auto:vocab", "worksheet": {"title": "Debate worksheet", "tasks": [{"instruction": "Translate to Korean.", "items": ["however", "therefore", "for example"], "key": ["하지만", "그래서", "예를 들어"]}, {"instruction": "Argue.", "items": ["The subway is handy. However, it's crowded", "For example, Seoul is big", "In short, the subway is good"], "key": ["지하철은 편리해요. 하지만 복잡해요", "예를 들어, 서울은 커요", "즉, 지하철이 좋아요"]}, {"instruction": "Add a point.", "items": ["Besides, the subway is cheap!", "In short, the subway is good"], "key": ["게다가 지하철이 싸요", "즉, 지하철이 좋아요"]}]}}]}, {"id": "B2-U3", "title": "Culture and mastery", "lessons": [{"id": "B2-U3-L1", "title": "Korean culture: 정 and food", "learn": "Culture time! 정 (deep affection/bond), 김치, 비빔밥, 한복 (traditional dress), 추석 (harvest festival). Have-tried: -아/어 봤어요: 김치를 먹어 봤어요? Guests first — 손님은 왕!", "vocab": [{"t": "김치", "r": "gimchi", "en": "kimchi", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "비빔밥", "r": "bibimbap", "en": "mixed rice", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "정", "r": "jeong", "en": "deep affection", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "한복", "r": "hanbok", "en": "traditional dress", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "추석", "r": "chuseok", "en": "harvest festival", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "설날", "r": "seollal", "en": "lunar new year", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "온돌", "r": "ondol", "en": "heated floor", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "태권도", "r": "taekwondo", "en": "taekwondo", "pos": "noun"}], "grammar": {"title": "-아/어 봤어요: have tried", "explain": "김치를 먹어 봤어요? (Have you tried kimchi?), 한복을 입어 봤어요 (I've tried hanbok)! 아/어 + 봤어요 = try-experience!", "pattern": "아/어 + 봤어요", "examples": [{"t": "김치를 먹어 봤어요?", "r": "gimchi-reul meog-eo bwass-eoyo?", "en": "Have you tried kimchi?"}, {"t": "비빔밥을 먹어 봤어요!", "r": "bibimbab-eul meog-eo bwass-eoyo!", "en": "I've tried bibimbap!"}, {"t": "한국에 가 봤어요.", "r": "hangug-e ga bwass-eoyo.", "en": "I've been to Korea. (tried going)"}], "mistakes": ["Saying 먹은 봤어요 — try needs 아/어: 먹어 봤어요!", "Saying 봤어요 for simple past — 봤어요 = tried/seen!"]}, "dialogue": [{"sp": "지훈", "t": "김치를 먹어 봤어요?", "r": "gimchi-reul meog-eo bwass-eoyo?", "en": "Have you tried kimchi?"}, {"sp": "미나", "t": "아니요! 먹어 보고 싶어요!", "r": "aniyo! meog-eo bogo sip-eoyo!", "en": "No! I want to try it!"}, {"sp": "지훈", "t": "비빔밥도 맛있어요!", "r": "bibimbab-do masiss-eoyo!", "en": "Bibimbap is delicious too!"}, {"sp": "미나", "t": "먹어 보고 싶어요!", "r": "meog-eo bogo sip-eoyo!", "en": "I want to try it!"}], "practice": [{"type": "translate_en", "q": "Say: Have you tried kimchi?", "answer": "김치를 먹어 봤어요?"}, {"type": "fill", "q": "먹어 ___ 싶어요! (want to try)", "answer": "보고"}, {"type": "choose", "q": "'I've been to Korea (tried going)' is…", "options": ["한국에 가요", "한국에 가 봤어요", "한국에 가고 싶어요", "한국에 갔어요 어제"], "answer": "한국에 가 봤어요"}, {"type": "reorder", "q": "Order: 봤어요 / 먹어 / 김치를", "answer": "김치를 먹어 봤어요"}, {"type": "speak", "q": "Say aloud: 김치를 먹어 봤어요?", "answer": "김치를 먹어 봤어요?"}], "quiz": [{"q": "먹어 봤어요 means…", "options": ["I eat", "I've tried eating", "I ate", "I can eat"], "answer": 1, "why": "아/어 + 봤어요 = tried."}, {"q": "먹어 보고 싶어요 means…", "options": ["I eat", "I want to try eating", "I ate", "I can eat"], "answer": 1, "why": "보고 싶어요 = want-to-try."}, {"q": "정 means…", "options": ["festival", "deep affection", "food", "dress"], "answer": 1, "why": "정 = warm human bond."}, {"q": "추석 is…", "options": ["new year", "harvest festival", "a food", "a dress"], "answer": 1, "why": "추석 = Korean thanksgiving."}, {"q": "한복 is…", "options": ["food", "traditional dress", "festival", "sport"], "answer": 1, "why": "한복 = traditional clothing."}], "flashcards": "auto:vocab", "worksheet": {"title": "Culture worksheet", "tasks": [{"instruction": "Translate to Korean.", "items": ["kimchi", "mixed rice", "deep affection"], "key": ["김치", "비빔밥", "정"]}, {"instruction": "Have tried.", "items": ["Have you tried kimchi?", "I've tried bibimbap", "I've been to Korea"], "key": ["김치를 먹어 봤어요", "비빔밥을 먹어 봤어요", "한국에 가 봤어요"]}, {"instruction": "Experiences.", "items": ["No! I want to try it!", "Bibimbap is delicious too!"], "key": ["아니요! 먹어 보고 싶어요", "비빔밥도 맛있어요"]}]}}, {"id": "B2-U3-L2", "title": "Storytelling: 옛날 옛적에", "learn": "Graduation! 옛날 옛적에 (long ago), 어느 날 (one day), 갑자기 (suddenly), 마침내 (at last), 마지막으로 (finally). Mix tenses: 갔어요, 먹고 있었어요, 먹고 싶어요! Tell YOUR Seoul story!", "vocab": [{"t": "옛날 옛적에", "r": "yetnal yetjeog-e", "en": "long ago", "pos": "phrase"}, {"t": "어느 날", "r": "eoneu nal", "en": "one day", "pos": "phrase"}, {"t": "갑자기", "r": "gapjagi", "en": "suddenly", "pos": "adverb"}, {"t": "마침내", "r": "machimnae", "en": "at last", "pos"